        "original_id": "5e3b038f-38f0-51ae-915b-62e3bd13d56a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Agee, Nelly Sachs, Davis Grubb\n- Works: A Death in the Family, The Night of the Hunter\n- Awards: Pulitzer Prize, Nobel Prize in Literature\n- Roles: film critics, screenwriters, novelists\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1940s, James Agee was one of the most influential film critics in the United States.\n- In 1953, Davis Grubb published the novel The Night of the Hunter.\n- In 1957, James Agee's autobiographical novel A Death in the Family was published.\n- In 1958, James Agee won a posthumous Pulitzer Prize for A Death in the Family.\n- James Agee wrote the screenplay for the film The Night of the Hunter, and it was based on Davis Grubb's 1953 novel of the same name.\n- In 1966, Nelly Sachs was awarded the Nobel Prize in Literature.",
